# Copy to `.env.local` and adjust. Next.js loads `.env.local` automatically.

# Base URL of the Trustify Trips customer API, including the /api suffix.
#
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is required: every call is made from the browser, so
# the value has to be inlined into the client bundle at build time. Changing it
# needs a restart in dev and a rebuild in production.
#
#   development   http://localhost:5000/api   (the default when unset)
#   production    https://api.trustifytrips.in/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORS — configured on the BACKEND, not here.
#
# This app runs on http://localhost:3000, which is a different origin to the
# API on :5000. Add it to the backend's own .env or every request fails in the
# browser before it reaches the server:
#
#   CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,https://trustifytrips.in,https://www.trustifytrips.in
#
# Note that http://localhost:3000 and http://127.0.0.1:3000 are different
# origins — list whichever the dev server prints, or both. A blocked origin
# shows up only as a console error; it never arrives as a status code in a
# catch block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#test commit